{%- comment -%}
  What a product is, read off its Unitee SKU, as one pipe-separated line:

    kind|garment|descriptor|gsm|fabric|fit|colour

  e.g. "hoodie|boxy hoodie|360 GSM Graphic Hoodie|360|100% cotton fleece|Boxy|Black"

  Unitee SKUs name the blank: 360-bl-hood-u-…, 240-offwh-boxy-tee-u-…,
  220-rd-baby-tee-u-…, 240-wh-ovr-waf-fs-u-… (GSM, colour code, blank).
  Fabric per blank is Unitee's own catalogue. Any part it cannot read is left
  empty, and a product that is not a Unitee blank gives an empty kind.

  Capture it and split on "|":
    {%- capture gf -%}{% render 'garment-facts', product: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign gf = gf | split: '|' -%}   (gf[0] kind … gf[6] colour)

  Used by the product page specs, the page title and meta description
  (layout/theme.liquid) and the product structured data (meta-tags).
  Params: product
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign sku = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku | downcase
  assign parts = sku | split: '-'
  assign gsm = parts.first | plus: 0
  assign kind = ''
  assign garment = ''
  assign descriptor = ''
  assign fabric = ''
  assign fit = ''
  if sku contains '-hood-'
    assign kind = 'hoodie'
    assign garment = 'boxy hoodie'
    assign descriptor = 'Graphic Hoodie'
    assign fabric = '100% cotton fleece'
    assign fit = 'Boxy'
  elsif sku contains 'baby-tee'
    assign kind = 'babytee'
    assign garment = 'baby tee'
    assign descriptor = "Women's Y2K Crop Tee"
    assign fabric = '95% cotton, 5% lycra'
    assign fit = 'Fitted'
  elsif sku contains 'boxy-tee'
    assign kind = 'boxytee'
    assign garment = 'boxy fit tee'
    assign descriptor = 'Boxy Graphic Tee'
    assign fabric = '100% French terry cotton'
    assign fit = 'Boxy'
    if product.title contains 'Denim' or product.title contains 'denim'
      assign garment = 'denim wash boxy tee'
      assign descriptor = 'Boxy Fit Tee'
    endif
  elsif sku contains '-waf-'
    assign kind = 'waffle'
    assign garment = 'waffle knit full-sleeve top'
    assign descriptor = 'Waffle Knit Graphic Top'
    assign fabric = 'Cotton blend waffle knit'
    assign fit = 'Oversized'
  elsif sku contains 'ovr-tee'
    assign kind = 'oversizedtee'
    assign garment = 'oversized tee'
    assign descriptor = 'Graphic Tee'
    assign fit = 'Oversized'
    if gsm == 240
      assign fabric = '100% French terry cotton'
    elsif gsm > 0
      assign fabric = '100% cotton'
    endif
  endif
  if gsm > 0 and kind != 'babytee' and kind != 'waffle'
    assign descriptor = gsm | append: ' GSM ' | append: descriptor
  endif

  comment
    Colour is the second part of the SKU when it is one of Unitee's codes.
  endcomment
  assign colour = ''
  case parts[1]
    when 'bl'
      assign colour = 'Black'
    when 'wh'
      assign colour = 'White'
    when 'offwh'
      assign colour = 'Off-white'
    when 'rd'
      assign colour = 'Red'
    when 'bpk'
      assign colour = 'Baby pink'
    when 'crm'
      assign colour = 'Cream'
    when 'gry', 'gr'
      assign colour = 'Grey'
  endcase
  comment
    Unitee's waffle knits come in off-white and black, so "wh" there is off-white.
  endcomment
  if kind == 'waffle' and colour == 'White'
    assign colour = 'Off-white'
  endif
  if gsm == 0
    assign gsm = ''
  endif
  echo kind | append: '|' | append: garment | append: '|' | append: descriptor | append: '|' | append: gsm | append: '|' | append: fabric | append: '|' | append: fit | append: '|' | append: colour
-%}
